%9Setting:%9

    backup_dir (path; default: ~/erssi-backups)

%9Description:%9

    The directory of the backups that backup_auto and /BACKUP NOW make.
    It is made (mode 0700) when it is not there yet. It must be outside
    the erssi home, also with its links followed: a backup there would
    hold all the ones before it, so erssi refuses it, says so and makes
    nothing. A directory that others can read
    shows them your backups: they hold your private keys and passwords.

%9Examples:%9

    /SET backup_dir ~/erssi-backups
    /SET backup_dir /backup/me/erssi

%9See also:%9 BACKUP, BACKUP_AUTO, BACKUP_KEEP
